; The Lathe-written linker (lathe/src/link.lth) banked on Wendy 2 run with `--disk DIR`
; (lathe/env/wendy2disk.env): files through lathe/rt/disk.lth (`PORTS 1`), the small build's
; tables (`LKSMALL 1`), code in three banks of the window by phase. lathe/tests/lk_banked.py builds
; and runs it; test_src_link.py compares what it writes with the host linker's; lk_bank_report.py
; measures it (lathe/host/README.md, "The linker in Lathe"; lathe/docs/spikes.md).
;
; The tables are in fixed memory, below the window and at $F810 and up, because code in the
; window cannot see a data bank in the same window. A table of more than 256 bytes is reached
; through its address (a fix-up of kind 2 and 3), so it is fixed even if one bank's code alone
; uses it; the small tables of a placed module go in its bank.
;
; Fixed: what every phase calls, many times: lk_tab, lk_rec, lk_sym, sys, disk and the run-time
; (rt_bank, rt_math), with lk_err's messages, the stubs and the start-up code, 9.9 KB.
; Bank 1, reading: link (main, which calls each phase once), lk_err (only on the way out), lk_file
; (only when a file is opened), lk_envf, lk_scan, lk_name. Bank 2, the graph and storage: lk_graph
; and lk_alloc, which reads the graph's columns through lk_graph's functions in its inner loops.
; Bank 3, placement and output: lk_place, lk_fix, lk_map, lk_emit, lk_out, lk_boot, lk_win and
; lk_op (only lk_emit uses it). The far calls that remain are about 3% of the cycles of a link,
; four fifths of them lk_fix, lk_map and lk_graph calling lk_name.global_sym and lk_fix calling
; lk_alloc.slot_addr, once a fix-up each (lk_bank_report.py).
;
; The split between variables and code is where both fit with room for a little growth: the
; variables ended at $58A4 (lk_name.local, the last large table, must end below the code; what
; follows it would go at $F810), and the fixed code at $7F66; the split went from $58C0 to $5940
; on 2026-11-20, when the environment's text grew by 128 bytes for the capacity variables' names
; of dynamic regions (lk_envf.TEXT_SIZE with LKDYN 1).
cpu       65c02
zeropage  $00 $FF
code      $5940 $7FFF
data      $0200 $593F
more      data $F810 $FFF9
stack     $FF
exit      stop
output    raw
window    WIN $8000 $EFFF
switch    WIN bank $F000 $1F
bank      WIN 1 $11 LINK1.BIN
bank      WIN 2 $12 LINK2.BIN
bank      WIN 3 $13 LINK3.BIN
place     link WIN 1
place     lk_err WIN 1
place     lk_file WIN 1
place     lk_envf WIN 1
place     lk_scan WIN 1
place     lk_name WIN 1
place     lk_graph WIN 2
place     lk_alloc WIN 2
place     lk_op WIN 3
place     lk_win WIN 3
place     lk_boot WIN 3
place     lk_fix WIN 3
place     lk_place WIN 3
place     lk_map WIN 3
place     lk_emit WIN 3
place     lk_out WIN 3
place     lk_dyn WIN 3
farcall   rt_bank
define    BOARD 2
define    DISK 1
define    PORTS 1     ; sys over the file ports (lathe/rt/disk.lth)
define    LKSMALL 1   ; the linker's tables at the small build's sizes
define    LKDYN 1     ; dynamic regions linked (lathe/src/lk_dyn.lth)
